 2. 👩‍💻 Outlook crawls back to life 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Microsoft says it's making progress in bringing its popular workplace software back online as a global outage reaches its second day.

 The outage, which has affected Outlook, Teams and AI assistant Copilot, has left millions of people, institutions and businesses worldwide without access to their email and other tools. 📧 Microsoft said today : "We're seeing encouraging recovery progress, with service availability and email delivery performance improving across a growing portion of affected Microsoft 365 infrastructure."

 The company added that users may have "intermittent access issues or delayed email delivery as mitigation progresses across the remaining affected infrastructure." 👾 The company hasn't fully explained the outage, but says there's no indication it was caused by malicious activity.

